    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d7">

                <pb facs="0119" n="5" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg5"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.00/2453: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Herod</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-03T14:00:00-04:40"><hi rendition="#italic">January 3,
                                1922—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 4—11:12
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1. The Military Governor<anchor n="2" xml:id="d7-f1"/> sailed today for
                    Washington with Commander Rose, Minister of Commerce. Last week the Admiral
                    conferred with Jacinto de Castro, Federico Velasquez, Francisco Peynado, and
                    Enrique Jimenez to (obtain?) agreement on plans of withdrawal and of warrant for
                    Guardia [National]. This conference proved fruitless.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herod</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
